From 1c5b6cf5d4c806f3c62fe2541412dfd4e03059f6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian MacDonald <ian@netstatz.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 18:28:02 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 077/104] docs(api): fix route spec lint and regenerate the API
 reference

gen_api_boilerplate.py --check failed on this branch: the API pages had
not been regenerated since the pull revision, beacon, health memory,
routing classify and images/classify changes, and several route specs
broke its rules. Statuses named in descriptions and notes move to the
errors tables, the classify, images/classify and routing/validate texts
fit the length limits, images/classify reads its arguments through their
RouteArg constants and gains a recorded example (MobileNetV2 on the image
fixture), routing/validate stops listing missing_argument, which its base
class no longer writes, and the generator's DISTINCT_ARGUMENTS and body
rules match the routes as they are.

